From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:43:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a PlatformScreen over the displays DRM reports

OzonePlatformDrm::CreateScreen() and InitScreen() were both NOTREACHED(). On
ChromeOS ash installs display::Screen itself and never asks for one; a views
browser on Linux goes DesktopScreenOzone -> ScreenOzone -> CreateScreen() and
hits them on startup, which is why the platform builds today but could not be
started. DrmScreen is what stands behind them.

It is modeled on HeadlessScreen rather than WaylandScreen, for the reason
docs/architecture/A-DESKTOP-ON-A-TTY.md gives: headless has no window-system
output protocol either, so it builds its display list from nothing, and DRM is
that shape with real snapshots in place of the fiction. Six of PlatformScreen's
nine pure virtuals are delegations to display::DisplayList and
ui/display/display_finder.h, and none of //ui/display/manager is ported --
DisplayChangeObserver spends 478 lines turning snapshots into ManagedDisplayInfo,
which is ChromeOS product surface that nothing here reads. The conversion this
needs is DisplaySnapshot -> display::Display directly, and it is three free
functions at the top of drm_screen.cc.

Two things that are not obvious from the interface:

A screen with no displays is not an answer PlatformScreen can give.
HeadlessScreen CHECKs its primary iterator and aura dereferences the result, so
"nothing plugged in" -- which is what all four connectors on the machine this
was written on report -- has to be a display rather than an empty list.
DisplaysFromSnapshots answers with one 1024x768 display in that case, and
clearing the NOTREACHED() without it would have moved the crash rather than
removed it.

DrmWindowHostManager::GetWindow() is NOTREACHED() on a widget it does not hold,
where every other ozone platform's manager returns null.
PlatformScreen::GetDisplayForAcceleratedWidget is handed widgets belonging to
other screens, so it cannot pass one through unchecked. HasWindow() is the
non-fatal lookup beside it, and it is the only edit this makes to a file
Chromium owns besides the two NOTREACHED()s and the BUILD.gn entries.

Hotplug needs no observer code: DisplayList notifies from AddOrUpdateDisplay and
RemoveDisplay, so OnDisplaysChanged replacing the list is the whole path.

The modeset driver that calls OnDisplaysChanged with real snapshots is the next
item in A-DESKTOP-ON-A-TTY.md's step 2; until it lands, InitScreen calls it with
none and the screen answers with the displayless display above.
